course: dictionary
lesson: 9286
title: One word, many shines
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word sparkle can mean more than one thing, and the words around it show you which meaning to use. «On an autumn morning, dew sparkles on dozens of round webs.» Dew shining with tiny bright flashes of light is the clue, so sparkles means shines in small, bright flashes.
explain: «It seems alive, chattering, chuckling, sparkling, and he sits on the bank, spellbound.» Chattering and chuckling are sounds of fun, so sparkling here means full of lively fun. The word is describing a feeling, not light.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does "shining with small bright flashes" fit? For the chattering sentence, "full of lively fun" fits better. If the swap makes no sense, read the words around it again.
fact: To sparkle means to shine with many small, bright flashes of light.
fact: A sparkle is a small, bright flash of light.
fact: Sparkle can also mean liveliness and fun in a person or a show.
fact: «Sparkling» drinks have bubbles, like «sparkling water».
fact: Stars, jewels, glitter and water in sunlight can all sparkle.
exercise: «On an autumn morning, dew sparkles on dozens of round webs.» What does sparkles mean here? | Falls slowly to the ground | *Shines with small bright flashes of light | Makes a loud noise | Melts away into nothing
exercise: «It seems alive, chattering, chuckling, sparkling.» What does sparkling mean here? | Wrapped in paper | Covered in dust | Made of glass | *Full of lively fun
exercise: Which phrase describes a drink with bubbles in it? | Warm milk | Still water | Cold tea | *Sparkling water
test: The sparkling drops on a sundew look like dew, but they are sticky. What does sparkling mean? | Covered in dust | Frozen solid | *Shining with small bright flashes of light | Quiet and still
test: «Add some sparkle to your story.» What does sparkle mean in this phrase? | A heavy rock | *Liveliness and fun | A loud bang | A dark shadow
exam: «Mia saw a sparkle on the lake.» What is a sparkle in her sentence? | A cold wind | A dark hole | A loud splash | *A small, bright flash of light
